      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "cGAS-STING supplied a central mechanism by which cytosolic DNA initiates innate immune signaling, with broad relevance to infection, autoimmunity, and cancer.",
        "attribution": "Chen is a central conceptual contributor; Ishikawa and Sun are appropriate proposed co-laureates for pivotal pathway work, though attribution is contested across a fast-moving field.",
        "maturity": "Core pathway biology has been replicated widely and integrated into innate-immunity research.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Clinical exploitation has not yet matched the clarity of the basic discovery.",
          "Priority and the appropriate limited set of contributors require careful historical assessment."
        ]
      }
    },
